resolve inside
executable file-backed bytes of a mapped segment rather than its zero-fill tail.
Legacy thread entrypoints must carry the complete ARM64 thread-state
flavor/count and a nonzero program counter; arbitrary
nonempty thread-command bodies do not qualify. Windows
images must also carry a complete COFF header, no deprecated image symbol-table
metadata, the executable-image characteristic without the DLL flag, and keep
the obsolete Windows working-set-trim characteristic zero while retaining
defined image flags. AMD64/ARM64 targets also reject the contradictory
32-bit-machine characteristic. They require a bounded
PE32+ optional header and section table with one to 96 sections whose virtual
addresses remain beyond the loaded header span, aligned, and adjacent by loaded
section span, a 64 KiB-aligned image base, and a
512–65536 power-of-two file alignment no larger than section alignment. Section
alignment below 4 KiB must equal file alignment, and nonempty section file
offsets must then equal their RVAs. Reserved loader fields remain zero,
including
Microsoft-reserved low `DllCharacteristics` bits, while defined
flags such as NX compatibility remain admissible. PE32+ image size stays at or
below Microsoft's 2 GiB image limit, and the declared image size matches the
final aligned loaded section span,
the header size matches the rounded header table, and the data directory count
must fit the optional header. Nonempty data directories must use a nonzero
address. Microsoft's Architecture and final Reserved directory slots must remain
